{
  "id": "EUVD-2025-27030",
  "enisaUuid": "58f78454-cc3d-3cc9-8eca-78fd89519fd9",
  "description": "There's a vulnerability in podman where an attacker may use the kube play command to overwrite host files when the kube file container a Secrete or a ConfigMap volume mount and such volume contains a symbolic link to a host file path. In a successful attack, the attacker can only control the target file to be overwritten but not the content to be written into the file.\n\nBinary-Affected: podman\nUpstream-version-introduced: v4.0.0\nUpstream-version-fixed: v5.6.1",
